  "body": "## What Happens\n\n`ImportModel::within` (crates/app/src/commands/import_model.rs, #2463) reads and parses the file, then reads the file a second time for its SHA-256. If the file changes between the two reads, the model holds the first bytes and the link records the second digest. The link check then sees no change. That change is never imported.\n\n## Steps To Reproduce\n\n1. Link a model to a file, or import the file.\n2. Change the file while the import parses it (a large model, one save during the parse).\n3. The model keeps the old geometry. Its operations do not go Stale. The status line says nothing.\n\n## Workaround\n\nSave or touch the file once more. The digest differs from the recorded one, and the check imports the file again.\n\n## What Should Happen\n\nRead the file once. Take the digest from the bytes that the parse used. `ImportModel::graded` already takes bytes in hand; use the same path for a file import.\n\n## Source\n\nFound in the review of PR #2563 (head `aef4f610c`), 2026-11-19. The code comment in `within` names the window. The window is one parse time.\n",
